You are auditing an agent-facing PROBLEM STATEMENT to ensure it is a FAIR test of whether an agent ANTICIPATES an edge case.

Setup: an earlier PR (PR1) introduced/changed behavior in {{ repo }}. A later PR (PR2) then fixed an edge case PR1 missed. We give an agent PR1's problem statement, have it solve PR1 from clean intent, and score whether its solution passes PR2's held-out tests — i.e. whether it ANTICIPATED the edge case WITHOUT being told.

For this to be fair the statement must sit in a Goldilocks zone:
- state the GOAL so a competent solution is possible;
- NOT prescribe the specific (flawed) implementation PR1 used — else following the task faithfully FORCES the bug, so the task contradicts the anticipation (UNFAIR);
- NOT reveal the edge-case handling PR2's tests check — else the agent is simply told the answer (LEAKY, anticipation becomes trivial).

